// Lots' categories (README, Lots). Each is [id, topic, difficulty, name, members, also, rule]:
//  - members: the words a lot is dealt from (more than four, so a lot is never the same four twice); WORD=note gives
//    the reason shown when the lot is opened (BEE=B), underscores in a note are spaces
//  - also: words that fit it too but are never dealt in it (a red herring's other home); @id takes in every word of
//    another category (every fish has scales)
//  - rule: "after:BALL" or "before:FIRE" for a phrase (FOOT·BALL, FIRE·WORK); "hidden:animals", "starts:", "ends:",
//    "anagram:", "front:" (a letter and a word), "back:" (a word and a letter) with one of the SETS below, and
//    "behead:" (a word of the set without its first letter), "palindrome", "novowel", "alpha" (letters in order): wordplay the page checks for itself, so any word on a board
//    that fits is counted, listed or not; "sound" for homophones; none for a set or a meaning.
// Difficulty: 1 a plain set anyone sees at once; 2 a set or a meaning that takes a moment, or a common phrase; 3 a
// specialist's set, a harder phrase, "things with", a homophone; 4 wordplay you have to spot, and the most devious.
// Ids are kept: a saved board names its lots by them. tests/lots.mjs checks every list (no word twice, more than four
// members, every rule's members fit it) and that every phrase lists every word of the bank that makes it.

